====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# An extravagant table [[ornament]] and [[container]] used in the [[Middle Ages]] and [[Renaissance]], made in the shape of a [[ship]].

====See also====
* {{l|enm|cadenas}}
* {{l|en|navicula}}

===Etymology 2===
Short for ''[[numerically]] [[effective]]''; introduced by Miles Reid.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}
{{wikipedia|Nef line bundle}}

# {{lb|en|algebraic geometry}} Of a [[line bundle]] on a complete algebraic variety over a [[field]]: such that the [[degree]] of its [[restriction]] to every algebraic curve in the [[variety]] is non-negative.
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Minimal Models of Canonical 3-Folds|author=Miles Reid|journal=Advanced Studies in Pure Mathematics|volume=1|year=1983|page=131|passage={{...}} this condition is the numerical consequence of the condition that for some <math>m > 0</math>, the linear system <math>|mD|</math> is effective and free; thus '''nef''' = "numerically (effective and free)".}}

